   "about": [
    {
     "title": "How the merge works",
     "html": "<ul><li><b>One journey, two stages.</b> Unverified clients are in the verification stage; verified clients</li></ul>\n<p>are in the funding stage. A verification, whenever it happens, moves the person straight to the funding stage (every “Wait for: verified” step’s Y output leads to A30).</p>\n<ul><li><b>Entry router.</b> At launch, and whenever a client enters late, Branch steps on verification</li></ul>\n<p>and registration date drop each person at the right point. Paths re-join, so shared steps exist once.</p>\n<ul><li><b>Reactions instead of fixed waits.</b> Quiet stretches are “Wait for a condition” steps. A login</li></ul>\n<p>during the funding stage triggers the “welcome back” email that day (old journey 06).</p>\n<ul><li><b>Variants by source.</b> Paid-social sign-ups and partner referrals get their own first email,</li></ul>\n<p>then join the main path. Paid social needs a CRM tag (<code>src-meta</code>), because UTM fields are not available inside a journey.</p>"
    },
    {
     "title": "Notes on the steps",
     "html": "<p>Steps A20, A30, A31 and A50 each receive connections from several places; that is what lets the stages share steps.</p>"
    },
    {
     "title": "Typical paths",
     "html": "<ul><li><b>Registers, verifies on day 1, funds on day 5.</b> S01-E1 → verifies → S03-E1 → S03-E2a → deposits</li></ul>\n<p>and leaves. Three emails.</p>\n<ul><li><b>Registers, verifies on day 10, never funds.</b> S01-E1, S01-E2b, S01-E3 → verifies → S03-E1,</li></ul>\n<p>S03-E2b, S03-E3 → no login → S04-E1 → login watch → exit around day 40. Seven emails. Journey B picks them up at day 90.</p>\n<ul><li><b>Never verifies, never opens.</b> S01-E1, S01-E2b, S01-E3, then silence (A17 skips the stalled</li></ul>\n<p>emails) → exit around day 63. Three emails.</p>\n<ul><li><b>Joined at launch, verified, registered 40 days ago.</b> Router → A33 → A50 → S04-E1 and the</li></ul>\n<p>login watch. One to two emails.</p>"
    },
    {
     "title": "New copy",
     "html": "<h4>S03-E1-B — subject-line variant for the A/B test at A37</h4>\n<p>Same body, button and footer as S03-E1. Only the subject and preheader change.</p>\n<ul><li><b>Subject:</b> Your account is ready to fund, from $10</li><li><b>Preheader:</b> Most payment methods are instant.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
     "title": "Needed in the CRM",
     "html": "<ul><li>Automation Rule: trigger “User registered”, condition UTM source equals “meta” → add client tag</li></ul>\n<p><code>src-meta</code>. Without it, steps A6 and A35 always take the N path, which is safe.</p>"
    },
    {
     "title": "Launch notes",
     "html": "<ul><li>At launch every client registered in the last 90 days who has not deposited enters at once. The</li></ul>\n<p>router spreads them across stages, but count the segment with “Preview audience” first.</p>\n<ul><li>A person can also be in journey G (failed deposit) at the same time. That is intended.</li></ul>"
    }
   ],
